WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
Two four-pixel patterns differ in the position of one active pixel.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
Averaging each pattern into one cell gives the same value: one quarter.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.550
If that position answered the question, the reduction already removed the needed evidence.

4
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.900
The columns are price and quantity; the row contains twelve and two.

5
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:36.067
A flat list retains the numbers but can lose which column each belongs to.

6
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:43.733
The correct structure means twelve euros per unit and two units, not the reversed interpretation.

7
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:51.083
Two voice traces contain the same words: “it is done”.

8
00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:57.933
One ends with a rising pitch contour and the other with a falling contour.

9
00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:05.983
The text matches but the prosody differs; no universal emotion is assigned to either contour.

10
00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:13.333
Video is sampled at seconds zero, two and four.

11
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:21.250
The light is on only between one and one and a half: no sample captures that interval.

12
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:28.600
Absence from the received frames does not prove the event never happened.

13
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:36.267
A flash and its sound belong to one event, but their recordings use different clocks.

14
00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:43.117
Audio appears three tenths of a second later on the video time scale.

15
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:50.467
Correcting the offset aligns the event; uncalibrated timestamps can invent an order.

16
00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:57.817
The camera reports eighty centimeters relative to its own origin.

17
00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:04.983
The map uses meters and its origin is twenty centimeters behind the camera origin.

18
00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:13.033
The same position is one meter in map coordinates: the reference changes, not the object.

